\begin_layout Subsection
Files isolation
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "Files-isolation"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Zones are defined by which files and directories processes running with them can access.
 Such isolation is provided by the Linux's kernel 
\series bold
mount namespace
\series default
.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Each zone thus has its own per user home directory,
 the 
\series bold
zone's user home directory
\series default
,
 in which all the user's files in that zone are located (the user has a different home directory in each zone even though the $HOME environment variable remains the same),
 where all his documents are stored.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Moreover,
 in order to be able to share files between zones,
 each zone's settings can also specify bind mounts which make files or directories either from other zones or from the actual home directory of the user in the Linux system appear in the zone.
 For example,
 if a user has to download some resources from the Internet before using them from a different work zone,
 the work zone could bind the Internet's 
\family typewriter
~/Download directory
\family default
 to the 
\family typewriter
~/Internet-downloaded-stuff
\family default
 directory (possibly read-only if necessary).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
So before the zone's 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

bubble
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 is set up,
 what will be the user home directory in the 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

bubble
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 is assembled as a temporary directory named 
\series bold
zone runtime home directory
\series default
 from the zone's settings.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
For example the following diagram shows:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
the actual home directory of the user in the system (bottom left) with the traditional XDG directories (like 
\family typewriter
Documents/
\family default
,
 and 
\family typewriter
Downloads/
\family default
 shown here),
 in an orange color;
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
a 
\series bold
zone's user home directory
\series default
 (top left) also with the traditional XDG directories,
 in a purple color,
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
on the right is the 
\series bold
zone runtime home directory
\series default
,
 built as follows:
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
the 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

root
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 is a bind mount of the zone's user home directory;
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
the 
\family typewriter
Documents/
\family default
 and 
\family typewriter
Dir_A/
\family default
 directories are binds from the the same directories in the actual home directory of the user;
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
the 
\family typewriter
Download/
\family default
 and 
\family typewriter
Dir_B/
\family default
 directories,
 not having been 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

overwritten
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 by a bind are from the zone's user home directory.
\end_layout

\end_deeper
