 with an embedded PADSI specific module which allows or denies DNS resolutions to proceed and logs events;
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
the 
\family typewriter
padsi-dns-server
\family default
 program which task is to (re)configure the unbound DNS server when the DNS server to forward requests to changes (as per the 
\family typewriter
/etc/resolv.conf
\family default
 file's contents) or when the filtering rules change (as per the 
\family typewriter
/etc/resolv-rules.json
\family default
 file's contents).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
the 
\family typewriter
padsi-dns-fw
\family default
 program which manages the configuration of the local firewall based on the configuration and the dynamic resolutions made by the 
\family typewriter
unbound
\family default
 DNS server.
 This program also loads the 
\family typewriter
/etc/resolv-rules.json
\family default
 file to extract network flow limitations in terms of protocols and ports.
