\begin_layout Paragraph
Resolution in the context of Virtual machines
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "VM-DNS"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
When a virtual machine is started in a zone,
 all the programs in the same zone can reach it using one of the following names:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\family typewriter
<nickname>.vm
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\family typewriter
<nickname>.<VM ID>.vm
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\family typewriter
<snapshot>.vm
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\family typewriter
<snapshot>.<VM ID>.vm
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
However,
 because one can start virtual machines from various definitions,
 to avoid name collisions,
 some of these names may already be used by previously started virtual machines.
 PADSI prevents this situation by removing duplicates.
 So for instance,
 if the user starts a Debian VM named 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

default
