\begin_layout Subsection
Infrastructure for the Web access
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "Web-infra"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This section describes the way PADSI tackles the following Web access needs:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
be able to use externals 
\series bold
Web proxies
\series default
 (popular in enterprises context to filter Web access) and yet also keep Web traffic filtering locally;
 and/or
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset


\series bold
Web redirection
\series default

\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 to indicate that a Web page access is denied and propose to open it in the same browser but in a zone which allows the access for better UX.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
If applications were allowed to directly ask an external Web proxy to connect to the target Web service,
 all the local network filtering to achieve network isolation could trivially be bypassed by a malicious actor (including for example to open SSH connections to an owned server).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
To avoid that security issue,
 PADSI:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
prevents direct access to the actual external Web proxies to use;
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
adds a local Web proxy
\begin_inset Foot
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Listening on port 3128.
\end_layout

\end_inset

 to enforce the network access restrictions (applications can use the 
\family typewriter
http://proxy:3128
\family default
 proxy setting when needed,
 e.g.
 in the 
\family typewriter
http_proxy
\family default
 and 
\family typewriter
https_proxy
\family default
 environment variables);
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
sets up the correct 
\family typewriter
http_proxy
\family default
 and the like environment variables and provides a WPAD web service
\begin_inset Foot
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Via the 
\family typewriter
http://wpad/wpad.dat
\family default
 URL.
\end_layout

\end_inset

 for programs to 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

auto-configure
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 them.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
These features (Web proxy,
 WPAD server and 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

Web redirection server
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

) are actually implemented using a single 
\series bold

\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

web-infra
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset


\series default
 application,
 which configuration depends on the zone's configuration.
 For the virtual machines,
 this proxy forwards requests to the associated zone's proxy.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\bar under
Notes
\bar default
:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
the WPAD server is enabled only when the Web proxy feature is enabled;
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
the 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

web page blocked
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 HTML contents and associated resources (like images) are served when appropriate.
\end_layout

