Other
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Printing
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
external mass storage handling
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
Side benefits
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The following problems happen to be solved by PADSI as side benefits:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
enterprises often struggle to prevent end users to multi-attach their endpoint to several networks (as the endpoint is the a 
\shape italic
de facto
\shape default
 router between the routers to which it is attached by network interfaces).
 In a PADSI system,
 being simultaneously attached to several networks is not a security risk as the endpoint's firewall blocks any strictly required network communications.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
end users and administrators are given a near complete visibility
\begin_inset Foot
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Except for legitimate network traffic which is not logged.
\end_layout

\end_inset

 into all the network traffic,
 in the 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

init
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 namespace,
 per zone and per administration namespace.
 Such information allows to adapt the network rules,
 lets users understand how programs behave almost in real time and security administrators be more efficient with regards to malicious communications.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
security services can be deployed and executed in an 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

area
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 where the end user (or any malicious software running with his privileges) has no reach,
 thus making it difficult or impossible for any malware to 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

kill
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 them (like EDR killers do).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Using PADSI
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This section highlights the various tools available to interact with PADSI.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection

\family typewriter
padsi-cli
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The 
\family typewriter
padsi-cli
\family default
 tool is the central command line tool to perform actions on a running PADSI instance (it does not allow one to create or modify the PADSI's configuration);
 it is for example used to create customized desktop entry files for programs (refer to section 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "Desktop-entries-monitor"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"

\end_inset

).
 This tool can be also executed from a zone even though it provides for much less (non required) features.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This tool can be used from a program outside of any zone (refer to section 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "Execution in the init ns"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"

\end_inset

) or from within a zone where it is limited to manage virtual machines in the zone
\begin_inset Foot
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Actually even though the program is still named 
\family typewriter
padsi-cli
\family default
,
 the actual programs are not the same.
\end_layout

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

