\begin_layout Subsubsection
Network resources sets
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "netres"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
A network resources set is a named collection of endpoints grouped into a single entity for easier maintenance.
 Network resources sets are defined in 
\family typewriter
.netres
\family default
 files which are in the JSON format where a key correspond to each network resources set which then is defined by:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\family typewriter
"descr"
\family default
:
 the network resource set's description (for easy maintenance);
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\family typewriter
"endpoints"
\family default
:
 a list of endpoints part of the network resources set,
 each an IP address or CIDR,
 or a domain name and possibly the transport means (TCP and/or UDP) and port numbers.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The network resources set to use MS365 can easily be built from Microsoft's own JSON definition using the 
\family typewriter
padsi-ms365-importer
\family default
 tool as follows:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
generate a UUID for the system (keep it in between downloads);
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
download the JSON file from 
\begin_inset CommandInset href
LatexCommand href
target "https://endpoints.office.com/endpoints/worldwide?clientrequestid=<uuid>"

\end_inset


\begin_inset Foot
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Refer to 
\begin_inset CommandInset href
LatexCommand href
target "http://aka.ms/ipurlws"
literal "false"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\end_inset

,
 e.g as the 
\family typewriter
worldwide.json
\family default
 file;
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
generate the 
\family typewriter
.netres
\family default
 file (e.g.
 as the 
\family typewriter
ms635.netres
\family default
 file):
 
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "basicstyle={\footnotesize\ttfamily}"
inline false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

padsi-ms365-importer create worldwide.json > ms365.netres
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Standard

\bar under
Note
\bar default
:
 the generated file contains several sections as provided by Microsoft like 
\family typewriter
ms365-common
\family default
 (Microsoft 365 Common and Office Online) or 
\family typewriter
ms365-exchange
\family default
 (Exchange Online) like in the example below.
\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Enumerate
integrate this file in padsi's configuration (the actual name of the file does not matter but its extension must be 
\family typewriter
.netres
\family default
);
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
reference the network resources sets in the zone's configuration files,
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This will for example produce the following (only a few lines shown):
\begin_inset listings
