\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

       Docs:
 man:sshd(8)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

             man:sshd_config(5)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

    Process:
 668397 ExecStartPre=/usr/sbin/sshd -t (code=exited,
 status=0/SUCCESS)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

   Main PID:
 668399 (sshd)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

[...]
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

# systemctl enable padsi-ssh@remote-access
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
Local administration
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The 
\family typewriter
padsi-do
\family default
 tool relies on sudo's configuration to operate,
 and as such,
 each user allowed to perform some local administration tasks must:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
be allowed to run 
\family typewriter
padsi-do
\family default
 (possibly limiting the name of the admin namespace to be used);
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
be explicitly allowed to run commands which will be executed by 
\family typewriter
padsi-do
\family default
,
 same as for 
\family typewriter
sudo
\family default
.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
For example,
 to give full admin privileges to the 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

john
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 user,
 one could create a 
\family typewriter
/etc/sudoers.d/padsi-sys-john
\family default
 file with the following contents:
\begin_inset listings
