\begin_layout Subsubsection
Unattended upgrades (Debian specific)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Debian's automatic updates deployment,
 the 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

unattended upgrades
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 feature,
 relies on a whole pipeline starting at some pre-defined intervals via the 
\family typewriter
apt-daily-upgrade
\family default
 systemd timer.
 For this mechanism to work on a PADSI system,
 the process run in the associated 
\family typewriter
apt-daily-upgrade
\family default
 service must be started in the admin namespace which provides adequate network access,
 like for example (where 
\family typewriter
theadminns
\family default
 is the admin.
 namespace to use):
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "basicstyle={\footnotesize\ttfamily}"
inline false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

ExecStart=/usr/bin/padsi-do --adminns theadminns /usr/lib/apt/apt.systemd.daily install
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

