\begin_layout Subsection
Locations of files used by a running instance
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The PADSI's service relies on both temporary files (mainly the zone's runtime files) and persistent files (user's files in the different zones,
 virtual machines' disk images,
 desktop entry and icon files,
 log files,
 ...).
 The runtime files are in the 
\family typewriter
/run/padsi
\family default
 directory (which is usually a temporary filesystem) whereas the persistent files are stored by default in the 
\family typewriter
/var/padsi
\family default
 directory.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
Runtime files
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Specifically,
 the 
\family typewriter
/run/padsi/
\family default
 directory contains the 
\family typewriter
user/
\family default
 directory for all per-user related data and the 
\family typewriter
zone-infos/
\family default
 directory for the information used by the GNOME Shell extension and other components to know which process is running in the context of which zone,
 and on which window it needs to add an outline and with which color.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The 
\family typewriter
/run/padsi/user/
\family default
 contains a sub directory per user's UID with an opened session,
 with the following sub directories:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\family typewriter
userfiles/<zone>/
\family default
:
 the user's home directory for each zone (assembled via bind mount points);
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\family typewriter
vm-management-files/<zone>/<vm ID>/<UUID>
\family default
:
 containing misc.
 files related to running virtual machines;
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\family typewriter
<object-type>-<UUID>/:

\family default
 containing all the run time files needed by the various components of the objects contributing to having a functional zone like Unix socket files and other run time files depending on the context.
 Object types are:
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
INFRA:
 infrastructure in support for a zone;
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
APPS:
 where a user's applications are actually running;
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
VM:
 infrastructure in support to run a virtual machine.
\end_layout

\end_deeper
