\begin_layout Subsection
D-Bus router
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Because a D-Bus client's 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

unique bus connection name
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 is assigned by the D-Bus server right after the connection is opened,
 the client receives its D-Bus address (it knows only one) from the first remote D-Bus server the D-Bus router connects to
\begin_inset Foot
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
In the case of screen sharing (but possibly for other use cases),
 the objects which are manipulated across D-Bus messages are derived from that connection name on the session bus,
 so the first remote D-Bus server the D-Bus router connects to must be the 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

real
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 session bus.
\end_layout

\end_inset

.
 The D-Bus router thus has to keep track of which bus connection name each client has,
 of which connection name each remote D-Bus server has assigned to each client,
 and perform some 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

translations
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 of addresses while messages are forwarded between the client and each remote D-Bus server.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The structure of the D-Bus is as follows:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
a global DBusRouter object listens for incoming connections on a Unix socket,
 authenticates each connecting client and creates 
\family typewriter
DBusClient
\family default
 objects as necessary;
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
each connected D-Bus client is handled by a 
\family typewriter
DBusClient
\family default
 object which:
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
receives messages from the D-Bus client and 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

routes
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 them to the appropriate remove D-Bus server based in the predefined rules and the 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

context
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

 (while opening connections to each remote D-Bus server,
 and authenticating to them),
 while falling back to a default D-Bus service;
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
analyses messages and extract relevant information into its 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

context
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 later used to route future messages (in the form of callbacks assigned to messages and called when the reply associated to the message is received);
\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
as required,
 each 
\family typewriter
DBusClient
\family default
 object opens a connection to a remote D-Bus server,
 and creates a 
\family typewriter
DBusRemoteService
\family default
 object to handle it;
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
