\begin_layout Standard
The following diagram help understand the situation where a D-Bus client (identified as 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

CLIENT-0
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

) connects to the D-Bus router and calls the 
\family typewriter
GetId()
\family default
 method on the 
\family typewriter
org.freedesktop.DBus
\family default
 interface of the 
\family typewriter
/org/freedesktop/DBus
\family default
 object of the 
\family typewriter
org.freedesktop.DBus
\family default
 service (the 
\family typewriter
/bubble/run/dbus-IH...O90
\family default
 is the name of a second D-Bus's Unix socket):
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
the client connects to the D-Bus router,
 calls the Hello() method,
 and get its connection name (
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

:1.434
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 here),
 the D-Bus router simply forwards the messages between the client and the 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

real
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 host D-Bus session;
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
the client calls the 
\family typewriter
Introspect()
\family default
 method which is 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

routed
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 to the other D-Bus service by the D-Bus router (based on its rules).
 Before forwarding that message to the selected D-Bus server,
 the D-Bus router opens a connection to that bus,
 calls the Hello() method,
 and catches the connection name assigned (
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

:1.0
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 here);
 this is done in the 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

say Hello()
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 frame;
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
the D-Bus router then sends the 
\family typewriter
Introspect()
\family default
 call message to the D-Bus server,
 and,
 when reply come,
 translates the destination address before relaying the reply to the client;
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
the client then calls the 
\family typewriter
GetId()
\family default
 method,
 and the D-Bus router simply 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

routes
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 messages back and forth while applying addresses translation.
\end_layout

