\begin_layout Itemize
the D-Bus router can allow client applications to own service names in the default (fallback) remote D-Bus bus and receive method calls vie D-Bus;
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
compared to 
\family typewriter
xdg-dbus-proxy
\family default
:
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize

\family typewriter
xdg-dbus-proxy
\family default
's role is to filter D-Bus calls to a single remote D-Bus service,
 it can't route between several remote D-Bus servers.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\family typewriter
xdg-dbus-proxy
\family default
 allows unlimited access to the session's bus service 
\family typewriter
org.freedesktop.DBus
\family default
,
 and more as specified by filters,
 the D-Bus router allows unlimited access bus the application can't choose which remote D-Bus server to use.
\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Paragraph
Debugging tips
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Refer to the following log files:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\family typewriter
/tmp/dbus-router.log
\family default
:
 contains all the inner events while handling messages,
 including the BASE64 encoded messages which can be analyzed using the 
\begin_inset CommandInset href
LatexCommand href
name "python-dbus-next"
target "https://github.com/altdesktop/python-dbus-next"
literal "false"

\end_inset

 module via some private objects,
 e.g.:
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "basicstyle={\footnotesize\ttfamily}"
inline false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

>>> from dbus_next._private.unmarshaller import *
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

>>> fd=open("msg.bin",
 "rb")
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

>>> u=Unmarshaller(fd)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

>>> msg=u.unmarshall()
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

>>> # analyse the msg object 
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
the log file can be visualized using the 
\family typewriter
dbus-logs-visu.py
\family default
 tool which will generate
\begin_inset Foot
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
This relies on the 
\begin_inset CommandInset href
LatexCommand href
name "PlantUML tool"
target "https://plantuml.com/"
literal "false"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\end_inset

 UML sequence diagrams in PDF files (the output being like the one above).
 For example:
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "basicstyle={\footnotesize\ttfamily}"
inline false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

$ dbus-logs-visu.py --out report.pdf /tmp/dbus-router.log report
\end_layout

\end_inset

 will generate a 
\family typewriter
report.pdf
\family default
 file,
 while
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "basicstyle={\footnotesize\ttfamily}"
inline false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

$ dbus-logs-visu.py /tmp/dbus-router.log list
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

20250519-09:17:07
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout

20250519-09:17:19
\end_layout

\end_inset

will list all the timestamps where some D-Bus events have been logged.
 Use this information to limit the size of the generated files via the 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset


\family typewriter
--since
\family default

\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 or 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset


\family typewriter
--until
\family default

\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 command line options.
